"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T22:18:13-07:00","id":1126977,"title":"","content":"Seriously that's lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:52:35-07:00","id":1127048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1115824-dark-eras-2-1001-nightmares-islamic-golden-age-thread?p=1118862#post1118862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's disappointing, sounds less like a setting and more like just recounts of various events like that Mary Shelly era from the companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that we still could still get a lot about the Era, according to a certain perspective. When it comes to the actual book, the 1001 says more about Islamic culture of the time than it says about Djinn and Roc birds. It's like Boccaccio's Decameron, stories the mirror the culture. A lot are also rather mundane.<br /> <br /> Could be wrong, though, that's for sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-10-2017, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:46:23-07:00","id":1127112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1115824-dark-eras-2-1001-nightmares-islamic-golden-age-thread?p=1126961#post1126961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm fairly certain that I'm going to use my expansion to add Mage to this era. If I don't change my mind. Again. Here's the pitch I wrote up in the main thread for this particular expansion:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Alot of that doesn't sound like it impacts directly upon the stories of 1,001 nights, except for Ibn Batuta, so I think you may be disappointed in picking that era. <br /> <br /> It really sounds like a strong focus on the 1,001 nights stories and their cultural impact, so its more akin to the Golden Age of Sci Fi then say the Cleopatra Era in DE2.<br /> <br /> In fact I've noticed a trend that while the splat focus has broadened, the era focus has narrowed, perhaps partly as a consquence. <br /> <br /> Examples, its Not simply Ancient Egypt: The Middle Kingdom, its Hawara and its Labyrinths. <br /> <br /> Its not simply carribean during a specific time period, its pirates!<br /> <br /> Its not just Europe during a specific times, its focused on reniance science.<br /> <br /> Its not just WW1, its WW1 the Western front.<br /> <br /> Its not simply the Hellenistic age, its the Wonders of the World!<br /> <br /> Its not just America before the civil war, its Steamboats, focused on well Steam Boats!<br /> <br /> Its not simply the Islamic Golden Age, its 1,001 stories.<br /> <br /> I just point this out because reading through your ideas alot of them are bold and great, but they don't really focus on the core them of the era, but more a broader exploration of an era.<br /> <br /> Example if someone picks Mummy for Wonders of the World, its going to be about sacred arcitecture and how mummies interact with the plans of the True Fae who are trying to control the wonders and the Prommy Pilgreams that visit them, its not going focus on say Romes invasion of Judea, or Mummies interacting with with Emperors and Pharohs of the time. Its about the Seven Wonders of the World and the Supernatural's interaction with them and each other, not about the broader Geopolitical situation of the age.<br /> <br /> You know what I mean? Each concept has a focused theme its wrapped around.<br /> <br /> Its just something concider when picking an era, how does your pick of splat impact on that core plotline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:20:56-07:00","id":1127136,"title":"","content":"The core theme is legends of the Islamic world. The backdrop to those stories is the cultural renaissance that was ushered in by the Abassid Caliphate and was continued by the Fatimids, Seljuks, C\u00f3rdoba Umayyads, and Shahs of Khwarazmia, among others. It is the fusion of Arabic and Persian culture, and the science that was generated through the fusion of east and west. Automata, waterworks, grand architecture... these are all a part do those legends and couldn't have happened without the progress made by the Abassids. Further, even though they aren't part of the 1001 Nights, the legends of the Assassins are persistent and world famous, for better or for worse. It fits perfectly with the theme of the era, even if they aren't technically part of the book the era gets is name from. <br /> <br /> Also... I haven't shown you my entire request, and I'm probably not going to. Suffice to say, there is latitude built into it. This part is meant to inspire, not be the be all and end all of what I want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a 